                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It looks nice and sounds a little intriguing, but that's all. Once you start playing you understand how buggy this game is, how empty the world is, how the unexplained story makes so little sense, how irritating the fact you can't save your progress is... Of course, this is just episode 1 of the whole game, but you can complete it in 15 minutes (achievement hunting included) and it doesn't seem like the devs are gonna continue with the rest of the episodes because episode 2 has been \"coming soon\" for 3 years already, ever since the release. And in my book bug-ridden 15-minute-long abandonware gets an instant thumbs-down, no matter how pretty it looks or that it costs a mere buck.",
